              <li><span>01</span><strong>Evidence image</strong><em>Map · manuscript · engraving · chain</em></li>
              <li><span>02</span><strong>Editorial kicker</strong><em>Category + method in compact UI type</em></li>
              <li><span>03</span><strong>Primary title</strong><em>Poppins, cream, sentence case</em></li>
              <li><span>04</span><strong>Gold emphasis</strong><em>One keyword or phrase only</em></li>
              <li><span>05</span><strong>Source metadata</strong><em>Quiet footer; never competing with title</em></li>
            </ol>
          </article>

          <article class="youtube-spec-panel">
            <header>
              <span class="hc-eyebrow">Hard Prohibitions</span>
              <h3>Do not import generic YouTube language</h3>
            </header>
            <ul class="youtube-donts">
              <li>No bright red arrows or oversized directional graphics.</li>
              <li>No neon outlines, glow text, or yellow marker effects.</li>
              <li>No reaction-face cutouts or exaggerated expressions.</li>
              <li>No giant all-caps verdict words competing with the title.</li>
              <li>No heavy drop shadows, glossy effects, or decorative gradients.</li>
              <li>Gold remains a signal color and stays within the brand's restrained footprint.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>

        <aside class="youtube-formula">
          <div>
            <span class="hc-eyebrow">Production Formula</span>
            <h3>Evidence → Title → Annotation → Source</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            A viewer should be able to identify the subject, read the claim, and understand that the image
            represents documentary evidence—all before the thumbnail is enlarged. The design communicates
            investigation, not spectacle.
          </p>
        </aside>
